{
	"_readme": [
		"Financial built-ins (FV IRR NPV PMT PV), array built-ins (FILTER SEQUENCE",
		"SORT TRANSPOSE UNIQUE) and SPARKLINE.",
		"",
		"The array functions return matrices, and this engine has no spill semantics.",
		"A spreadsheet spills the matrix across neighbouring cells and shows its",
		"top-left value in the anchor cell, so `expected` for a bare array call is",
		"that top-left value. Every such fixture is a known-failure carrying the raw",
		"matrix as `actual`; together they measure the size of the missing feature.",
		"Calls that CONSUME a matrix (SUM, INDEX, ROWS, COLUMNS) work and are",
		"recorded as passing, because that is the composition the engine does support.",
		"",
		"SPARKLINE returns a render-only spec object rather than a value. The object",
		"cannot be compared through JSON, so these fixtures assert the surrounding",
		"contract instead: the spec must never reach the user as '[object Object]'.",
		"The spec's own shape is asserted in formula.functions.lookup.test.ts.",
		"",
		"Wrong-argument-count cases use Google Sheets as the oracle: Sheets surfaces",
		"'Wrong number of arguments' as #N/A, while Excel refuses the formula at entry."
	],
